WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.864
NOT EXISTS expresses the anti-match directly For
each patient the

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.616
inner query searches for a review-queue row with the
same patient ID If

00:00:11.642 --> 00:00:17.368
no matching row exists the patient is kept The
unrelated NULL row

00:00:17.381 --> 00:00:21.697
does not create the same problem because it does not
match the current patient ID

00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:27.964
This is why NOT EXISTS is often the clearer starting
point for anti-join questions
